# AFS Cursor Rule

- Read `AGENTS.md`, `COMPANY.md`, `PRODUCT.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `LOOPS.md`, `TASTE.md`, and
  `GAPS.md` when relevant before changing behavior, product direction,
  knowledge, or subjective quality.
- Keep raw material in Google Drive; provenance in `SOURCES.md`; references in `REFERENCES.md`.
- Do not create `official-documentation/`.
- Put live facts in `facts/<domain>/`, and technical how-to guides in `cookbooks/`.
- Keep goals in Notion, guided by `ROADMAP.md`; templates beside their content.
- Keep unique knowledge in `knowledge/` and research units in `research/<unit>/`.
- Keep large root-style Markdown files out of legacy `context/`.
- Add unresolved knowledge or understanding gaps to `GAPS.md`.
- Prefer updating durable AFS files over burying reusable context in chat.
